+### Fate compatibility patch: bounded aggregate run results
+
+`Agent.runHistoryMode` / `AgentOptions.runHistoryMode` / `AgentLoopConfig.runHistoryMode` defaults to `"all"`. The explicit `"last-turn"` mode retains only the current completed turn in the aggregate `agent_end.messages` (and low-level loop return value). `agent_end.runHistory` then states the mode and exact omitted message count. It does not change model context, queues, tool execution, per-message/per-turn events, requests, or persistence. A host choosing this mode must persist originals via the existing per-message lifecycle and use those originals for full-run audit; never interpret the event tail as the whole history. Hook consumers of `AgentTurnContext.newMessages` see the same bounded aggregate. The mode is fixed at loop start and does not impose a model/run budget.
